    "concept_4": {
      "id": "concept_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The book also links three bases through multiplication.\n\nIf 2^x = 3^y = 6^(-z) = k, then 2×3=6 gives:\n\nk^(1/x) × k^(1/y) = k^(-1/z).\n\nSo 1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
